          "text": [
            "DISCRETE GAUSS–BONNET  Σᵥ (2π − Σθ) = 2πχ\n    tetrahedron\n      V =  4   E =  6   F =  4    χ = V−E+F =  2\n      Σ Kᵥ =  12.566370614359172      2πχ =  12.566370614359172\n      difference =  0.0\n    octahedron\n      V =  6   E =  12   F =  8    χ = V−E+F =  2\n      Σ Kᵥ =  12.566370614359176      2πχ =  12.566370614359172\n      difference =  3.552713678800501e-15\n    icosahedron\n      V =  12   E =  30   F =  20    χ = V−E+F =  2\n      Σ Kᵥ =  12.56637061435918      2πχ =  12.566370614359172\n      difference =  7.105427357601002e-15\nExact in every case, at four vertices as much as at twelve.  3.08\nneeded a smooth surface and an integral; this needs neither, and\nthe proof is a count of angles: every triangle contributes π to the\ntotal angle sum, so Σθ = πF, and 2πV − πF = 2π(V − E + F) once\n3F = 2E is used."
